From: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v4] kpatch-build: skip unreconcilable 6.12.95 objects

Two objects in the 6.12.95 vpsadminos build cannot be processed by
create-diff-object:

  - kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o: the changed functions of the accepted
    ring-buffer row (6d666f0b8b36, recreated as bc8f306b) have no
    patchable function entries in the boot vmlinux - their prologues are
    plain "push %rbp; mov %rsp,%rbp" where a patchable function starts
    with "call __fentry__" (contrast the carried
    __x64_sys_perf_event_open).  The row is carried boot-only with the
    native 6.12.110 ancestry, not by the online 6.12.95 payload.
  - drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o: a faithful two-sided
    rebuild shows identical code, rodata, relocation and symbol tables;
    only debug line-number data differs.  Zero changed functions.

Two BPF-side header fan-out objects also contain no patchable content:

  - net/bpf/test_run.o and kernel/bpf/helpers.o contain only debug,
    BTF-ID and unselected init-text bookkeeping differences.  Neither is
    a direct payload object or contributes a changed function.

An earlier revision also skipped net/core/filter.o.  With the exact
producer inputs, create-diff-object now returns its normal no-difference
status and emits no diff object for that original/patched pair.  Leave it
on the normal create-diff-object path so any later functional difference
cannot be hidden by an early skip.

Skip the four remaining objects the same way usr/initramfs_data.o is
skipped.

Development history:

  v2: Record the boot-only ring-buffer disposition and the exact
      debug-only t4_hw.o classification.
  v3: Add the three BPF-side header fan-out objects that the then-current
      create-diff-object could not reconcile.
  v4: Remove filter.o from the early skip after exact retained-object
      admission proved the pinned producer reports no functional diff.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Snajdr <snajpa@snajpa.net>
---
 kpatch-build/kpatch-build | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
+++ b/kpatch-build/kpatch-build
@@ -1445,6 +1445,13 @@
 		[[ "$i" = arch/x86/lib/copy_user_64.o ]] && continue
 
 	[[ "$i" = usr/initramfs_data.o ]] && continue
+	# Objects that create-diff-object cannot reconcile on the 6.12.95
+	# base and that contribute no patchable functions to this module;
+	# ring_buffer.o's row is carried boot-only, t4_hw.o is debug-only.
+	[[ "$i" = kernel/trace/ring_buffer.o ]] && continue
+	[[ "$i" = net/bpf/test_run.o ]] && continue
+	[[ "$i" = kernel/bpf/helpers.o ]] && continue
+	[[ "$i" = drivers/net/ethernet/chelsio/cxgb4/t4_hw.o ]] && continue
 
 	mkdir -p "output/$(dirname "$i")"
 	cd "$BUILDDIR" || die
